[PLAN] feat.compile.when_import: A `when` condition resolves a predicate call where its declaration is written (design principles 5.13, 10.2): the module's own names, then what its imports bring (a module prefix, a selective import, an alias), then the prelude. An imported predicate is instantiated and constant-folded exactly as a local one; a name that is not a predicate, two imports of one name, and a predicate in a module that is not imported each have their own report.
