[PLAN] feat.compile.param_defaults: Defaults of ordinary parameters and ordinary arguments given by name (design principles 4.4, handover H276): one rule with the `with` parameters — a default is a compile-time constant evaluated where the declaration is, and a call gives the parameters by position, or by name after the positional ones, in the declaration's order. A callee that is several declarations names the parameter at each position the same way in all of them, and a name then means one position there (handover H376); a call of such a callee fills no default, since a default is written by one declaration.
