[PLAN] feat.modules.rules_libraries: The first two standard rule libraries (rewrite design 2 (second version) 8.9-8.10): `rules::accuracy`, which turns a log of a softmax and the scalar `log(1+x)`/`exp(x)-1` forms into the accurate operators on licensed functions, and `rules::fusion`, which turns the sigmoid chain 1/(1+exp(-x)) into the sigmoid kernel. The naive softmax and naive log-softmax are deliberately absent: `check` measures the first as worse on f32 and the case `check_rejected_softmax` pins the refusal. Each accepted rule is shown firing with its rewrite count and operator cost, on programs it must not match, and with the same bits on nvm, fvm and jit.
